// ── Reference-resolver classifier tables (`EbGetExpressionType2`) ─────────────
//
// The expression-type classifier indexes two tables. Both abut another table in
// the DLL, and the accessors mask/scale the index past the logical table's end,
// so the genuine extent is the *accessor range*, not the table-symbol distance:
//
//  * `RT_RESOLVER_CLASS_FLAG` (`DAT_0fab5b10`): the logical class-flag table is
//    0x28 bytes, but the accessor index is `pcode_opcode & 0x3f` (0..0x3f), so a
//    low-6-bits value >= 0x28 reads on into the adjacent call-convention records.
//    The window stored here is the exact 64-byte memory image — bytes 0x28..0x3f
//    coincide with [`RT_CALL_CONV_RECORDS`] (@0fab5b38), reproduced so an opcode
//    with low6 >= 0x28 reads the same byte the DLL would.
//  * `RT_RESOLVER_TYPE_MAP` (`DAT_0fc10aa8`): the logical type-map is 0x28 bytes,
//    but the accessor index `(local_c + (b1 & 7) * 3) * 2 + (b2 & 7)` reaches a
//    maximum of 0x35 (local_c<=2, the two nibbles <=7), so 54 bytes are stored.
//    Bytes 0x28..0x33 coincide with [`RT_CALL_TYPECODE`] (@0fc10ad0); 0x34/0x35
//    are the two trailing bytes the accessor can still reach.

/// `DAT_0fab5b10` — the resolver class-flag table, the full 64-byte window the
/// `& 0x3f` accessor can read (logical table is the first 0x28 bytes).
